      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Aberration-corrected electron microscopy opened routine direct access to atomic-scale structure and has reshaped materials science.",
        "attribution": "Rose supplied key correction theory, while Haider was central to practical realization; the technical chain is unusually identifiable.",
        "maturity": "The method is long established, widely replicated, and indispensable across microscopy laboratories.",
        "uncertainties": [
